> Derek Ray wrote:
>> This is begging the question; why should Magicbane _not_ appeal to Rogues?
>
> Because it's a wizard specific weapon.

No.  It's an artifact dagger that happens to be the wizard's first
sacrifice gift.  If it was intended to be "wizard only" it would be a
Quest Artifact.

> Only valks really care about that shocking hammer and with your latest 
> changes Demonbane is interesting for priests but not so much for other 
> classes.

Neither of these are accurate assumptions.  More roles can get gifted
Mjollnir than just Valkyries, and more roles can get gifted Demonbane
than just priests.

For someone who was conducting a sacfest, receiving either of these
weapons should certainly be better than whatever ordinary weapon they
had on hand; perhaps it isn't their first choice for ascension, but if
you really want your ideal choice guaranteed, you can either play the
classes that get a good one first-gifted (wizards, barbarians), or you
can wish it up.

> Currently Magicbane is the uberweapon for Rogues 

This is a personal opinion, not objective fact; you are basing it solely on
Magicbane supporting the style you believe works best.  It is still very
much up in the air whether that style _is_ most efficient for ascending,
though; results so far indicate that it's not.

You can find people who consider Frost Brand + a silver saber to be equally 
"uber"; you can probably even find Stormbringer adherents out there as well,
strangely enough.  And you can find those who wish for Grayswandir even
though it'll zap them at every turn.

> the other twoweapon classes while mostly just a useful writing tool for 
> wizards.  (A wizard has to sacfest early to have Magicbane as their most 
> effective means of attack.)

So what wizards again exactly _don't_ stop and sacfest early?  Every one I
know does -- and in Spork there's an added incentive since wizards no
longer start with built-in MR.

> Rogues could still cast Sleep or use a wand or something to line up a 
> target for a sleeping backstab, but as long as scare works it makes 
> standing on an E-graving very very useful for them.  

While this is true, you're still not answering the question of why this
should be changed in the first place.  If I went around trying to stomp
on everything that was just 'useful', I would rapidly end up with DeathHack,
where the player ineffectually flailed at arch-liches and jabberwocks on
DL1 with his starting rubber hose.

I see no particular excessive advantage that Rogues have WRT standing on
Elbereth and stabbing away with Magicbane.  Yes, they get backstab
bonuses.  That would be one of the advantages they're SUPPOSED to get.

> Rogues also have the top secret advantage over tourists of non-hostile 
